# Presentation

This folder contains presentation materials for the SmartCare Hospital AI coursework (CCS3440).

## Contents

- **slides.pptx** — Presentation slides summarizing the project: problem definition, methodology, results, and conclusions.
- **video_demo.mp4** (or link) — 5–10 minute video demonstration of the AI prototype in action, as required by the coursework submission checklist.
- **screenshots/** — Screenshots of the working prototype (Streamlit/Flask app) showing user input, predictions, and results display.

## Presentation Outline

Slides should generally follow the structure of the technical report:

1. **Title Slide** — Project name, group members, module code (CCS3440)
2. **Introduction & Problem Definition** — Selected prediction task (No-Show / Readmission / Disease Risk)
3. **Literature Review Summary** — Key findings from reviewed papers, research gap
4. **Dataset Overview** — Description of `smartcare_ai_dataset_1000.csv`, key attributes
5. **Data Preprocessing & Feature Engineering** — Key decisions and justifications
6. **Exploratory Data Analysis** — Key visualizations and insights
7. **Model Development** — Models trained (minimum 3), hyperparameters
8. **Model Evaluation** — Comparison table, best-performing model
9. **Explainable AI Analysis** — SHAP/LIME/Feature Importance insights
10. **Prototype Demo** — Screenshots or live demo walkthrough
11. **Results & Discussion**
12. **Conclusion & Future Work**
13. **References**

## Notes

- Keep slides concise — use visuals (charts, tables, screenshots) rather than dense text blocks.
- Ensure every group member can individually explain their contributions, as this ties into the Viva Examination component.
- Video demonstration should walk through the prototype accepting input, generating a prediction, and displaying results.
- Align slide content with the final Technical Report (Task 09) to keep the story consistent.
